What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_band
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_band
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Select the frequency band of the channel, when the channel is
		served by separate signal chains, each covering a frequency
		band. Valid values are listed in the corresponding
		_band_available attribute. If the channel is disabled, the
		selection may only take effect once it is enabled.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_band_available
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_band_available
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of frequency bands supported by the channel, for example
		"low" and "high".

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_sideband
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Select which mixing product of the local oscillator (LO)
		channel is kept at the mixer output: "lower" for the product
		below the LO frequency, "upper" for the product above it. The
		other product is rejected as the image.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_sideband_available
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of supported sidebands: "lower" and "upper".

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_i_calibphase
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_q_calibphase
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Unscaled phase calibration of the in-phase (I) or quadrature
		(Q) component of the channel, used to correct quadrature phase
		imbalance, for example to improve image rejection.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltageY_calibbias_calibration
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Write 1 to run the automatic offset calibration of the channel,
		for example LO leakage nulling of a local oscillator (LO)
		channel. The offsets found by the calibration are applied by
		the device, and may not be reflected in the calibbias
		attributes of the channel components. Writing one of those
		attributes afterwards replaces all the calibrated offsets of
		the channel with the values of those attributes. Returns -EBUSY
		if the device is not in a state where the calibration can run.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_hardwaregain_lut_en
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Enable (1) or disable (0) the device lookup table (LUT) for the
		gain settings of the channel. The LUT contents and their
		configuration, such as the LUT pointer source, are loaded through
		the firmware upload interface of the device. While the LUT is
		enabled, the gains follow the selected LUT entry, and the
		hardwaregain attribute of the channel returns -EBUSY. Enabling a
		LUT that has not been loaded returns -ENODATA.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/filter_lut
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Select the active page of the device lookup table (LUT) for the
		filter (frequency) settings, or "off" to disable it. The contents
		and configuration of each page are loaded through the firmware
		upload interface of the device. While the LUT is enabled, the
		settings it controls follow the selected LUT entry, and the
		channel attributes that access those settings return -EBUSY.
		Switching pages while the LUT is enabled is immediate, and only
		the inactive page can be loaded, allowing one page to be updated
		while the other is in use. Selecting a page that has not been
		loaded returns -ENODATA.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/filter_lut_available
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of filter LUT settings: "off", and the LUT pages, for
		example "a" and "b".

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_filter_low_pass_raw
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_filter_high_pass_raw
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Unscaled setting of a controllable low pass or high pass
		filter applied to the channel, for filters whose cutoff
		frequency is not characterized for each setting, so that
		filter_low_pass_3db_frequency or filter_high_pass_3db_frequency
		cannot be provided. How the setting relates to the cutoff
		frequency is device specific. The valid settings are given by
		the corresponding _available attribute.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_filter_low_pass_raw_available
What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltageY_filter_high_pass_raw_available
KernelVersion:	7.5
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Range of valid unscaled filter settings, given as
		[min step max].
